WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.750
- Well, good afternoon, everybody

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.100
and thank you for attending.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.300
My name is Paul Murawski
and I head up Marketing

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.650
and Trademark Licensing
here at Yale University.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.219
I'd like to first thank
the IT folks for asking me

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.890
to speak a little bit about my department

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.420
and you're probably all
wondering, why am I gonna speak,

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.050
what does marketing or
licensing have to do,

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.290
but actually, because
we manage the Yale marks

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.410
on a university basis,
we touch all departments

00:00:36.263 --> 00:00:39.283
in one way, shape or form
over the course of a year.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.700
But before I start, just
to give you a little bit

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.510
about my background, I
have been fortunate enough

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.680
to work at Yale for about three years.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.040
I have been in the marketing

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.010
and licensing business my
entire life, about 40 years.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.450
I come primarily out of
department store world,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.190
with 17 years in department stores

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.850
and I've had my own consulting business,

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.610
and prior, also headed
Licensing and Retail

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.363
for the American Museum of
Natural History in New York City.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.260
At Yale, I've, like I
said, been here three years

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.480
and I also sit on the Yale Committee

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.940
for Cooperative Research.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.650
What I'd like to do is take
you through a little bit

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.630
about what we do and,
basically, it comes down

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.430
to three issues that
my department handles.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.360
First is we take care of
protection of the Yale marks,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.910
secondly, we try to establish
a marketing platform

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:30.270
for the Yale brand globally,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.610
and third, we manage the licensing

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.630
so that we actually bring
in additional revenue

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:39.230
to the University through
the licensing contracts

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.640
that we provide.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.760
And just to start with,
I thought I'd give you

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.610
a little overview of some of the things

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.370
that we do regarding
protection of brands, things

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:49.800
that we look at in order to make sure

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.900
the Yale brand is managed appropriately,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.390
and the people that we find
we have the most concerns

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.510
with are, a lot of times,

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.700
outside contractors will
wanna use the Yale name

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.750
because they've done construction on Yale,

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.360
or they've produced a book
for Yale, or whatever.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.820
So, what they like to do is they like

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.300
to take the Yale name,
put it on their website.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.710
Well actually, you can't do that.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.033
That's actually illegal.

00:02:10.915 --> 00:02:12.730
It's actually a misuse of trademark.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.060
So, we run into a lot of those issues.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.900
We run into issues

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.200
with the power companies
misusing our names.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.330
We've run into that, especially, overseas.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.840
Recently, in Taiwan and in mainland China.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.870
There's also been a case

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.490
where a company was
using Yale Kindergarten,

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.920
which, obviously, they can't do.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.760
So, there's a lot of
different things that we try

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.890
to get in front of so that
the problems don't occur

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.530
and that we can actually
make it so it's easy

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.400
for the people who can use the Yale marks

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.150
to do it appropriately.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.400
So first, what we've
done is we put some pegs

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.740
in the ground, some guidelines

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.610
for how to use the Yale brands, starting

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.760
with outside consultants and contractors,

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.180
and the most important thing there is

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.000
that, basically, it's not allowed.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.810
You can't promote, sponsor, approve

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.380
of outside consultants or contractors,

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.140
or any goods or services, regardless

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.920
of the relationship with Yale.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.300
So, it doesn't matter who the
company is, how big they are,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.620
they can't use the Yale brand

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.930
because Yale is a
not-for-profit institution

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:14.530
and it cannot seem as
endorsing a corporate venture

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.910
related to commerce.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:20.920
So secondly, the other area we
target is, are the students.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.510
We love our students and
they're very creative

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.070
in the way they wanna use the Yale marks,

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:25.980
and it's very interesting

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.370
to see some of the things
they come to us with.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.910
But, so what we wanted to do is we wanted

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.980
to create, put pegs in the
ground for the students

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.400
so they clearly understood
how to use the Yale mark,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.933
but also not to crimp their
creativity, shall we say,

00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:40.610
because you should see some of the things

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.570
that come across our
desk when it comes time

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.340
for the Harvard football
games or some of the events

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.040
that the students run in the dorms.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.930
So, we have to be cautious of that.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.410
So, what we've done is we
put together a guideline

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.710
for the students.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.420
It was spurred on by the
Secretary of the University,

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.340
who has the actual rights to
use the marks as she see fits,

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.370
or her authorized agents,

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.620
which happens to be our department.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.390
So, any student group that wants

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.760
to use the Yale name has to first register

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.330
with a student organization,
whether it's undergrad or grad,

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:17.330
to make sure they are a legitimate
entity of the University.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.260
And also, they have to
make sure they comply

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.010
with the University's standards

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:25.360
regarding the guidelines
associated to use of the marks.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.690
And we've established these,

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.860
along with the Office of General Counsel,

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.280
and they include things like your logo

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.440
and name must identify you
as a student organization.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.330
You have to convey that in any way

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.140
that you present your organization.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:44.080
That includes on your
emails, on your website,

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.080
on any paraphernalia or
swag that you wanna buy.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.520
So, you have to convey
that student affiliation,

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.503
which you see some examples here.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.527
Secondly, a lot of students say,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:58.670
"Well, I can convey my affiliation by Yale

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.377
by saying 'at Yale,'"
but actually, you can't.

00:05:01.377 --> 00:05:04.190
"At Yale" is tied to The
Shops at Yale downtown,

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.370
so you can't use "at Yale."

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.520
That does not allow you to comply

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.450
with the idea of being
a student organization

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.193
in relationship to the University.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.440
Use of logos, this is
always very interesting

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.280
because this is where
the students get creative

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.050
and, certainly, we encourage that,

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.360
but things like you have to indicate

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.700
that you're a student organization,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.860
like the Yale Undergraduate
Chamber Orchestra.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.190
The two groups of marks
that are labeled able to use

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.110
are the Yale Block and the Yale "Y,"

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:36.390
but when using those two
logos, you cannot alter them.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.150
So, in other words,
when we get, let's say,

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:41.990
swag for an event that one of
the colleges are going to use,

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.210
they can present it to
us, they can say Yale,

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.453
but they can't alter those two marks.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.130
Also acronyms, if you use
an acronym, you also have

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.990
to indicate that you're
a student organization,

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:52.963
as you see here.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.260
And items to be distributed,
this is my favorite.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:00.100
So, if you use the word Yale

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.880
in your name and logo,
you also have to include

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.060
that you're a registered
student organization.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.430
So, you see here the Yale Refugee Project.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.880
Underneath it, it says an
undergraduate organization,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.510
which is very important to note,

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:15.550
because what you have to
think about is a student

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.810
from one of the colleges
puts together a t-shirt

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.360
that has something that is,
could be considered offensive.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.370
That student goes to New York City

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.780
on a Friday night, goes to
Grand Central Station, is seen

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.670
by thousands of people.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.230
That's the image that
Yale's now portraying

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.800
to the world out there.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.150
So, we have to be very cautious,

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:35.260
and when we look at something

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.410
in my department, it's
how does the world see it?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.150
How is John Q. Public gonna
see Yale in that context?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.650
And that's how we judge whether
it's appropriate or not.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.100
And, of course, the one thing we also keep

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.170
in mind is you can't use
orange and you can't use red

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.661
because you don't wanna
be Princeton or Harvard.

00:06:50.661 --> 00:06:52.850
(people in audience laugh)
But anyway,

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.410
so websites, that's another favorite.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.540
Actually, we run into
this issue more than any

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.230
because it's really not that
students wanna do it wrong,

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.690
they just don't understand the guidelines

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.080
associated with that.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.760
So, something like making
sure you have your logo

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:08.060
conspicuously on the website.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.590
And, importantly, you
have to have a disclaimer,

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.620
because every student organization
is also insured by Yale,

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.570
so having that disclaimer is important

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.870
to let it know that it's
a student organization,

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:21.050
not a Yale University organization.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.790
And also, the email addresses associated

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.710
to that have to be Yale email addresses.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.410
You can't do gmail@Yale.com.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.330
That's not allowed if you're
a student organization.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:33.230
You have to tie to whatever email address

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:36.173
that the student in
charge of the group has.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.920
So now you think about, okay,

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.340
now you can do the brand protection,

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.400
very important part of it.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.070
This is an idea, last year

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:48.070
in fiscal 2018, we actually
dealt with 144 cases, globally,

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.510
of misuse of the Yale marks.

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:53.060
That's across the world.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.460
Majority here in the United States,

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:58.020
but also we ran into in
Asia, we ran into in Europe,

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.610
ran into it in the Middle East.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:02.710
So, those types of things
all come across our desk.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.670
So, the idea is, say, okay,
what does Yale Licensing have

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:06.503
to do with that?

00:08:06.503 --> 00:08:09.070
But, if you think about it
for a minute, if we're able

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.370
to market the Yale brand properly,

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:14.730
and we get it out there in
as many venues as possible,

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.620
people are gonna see, it's
gonna become more popular,

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:17.459
it's gonna become more important,

00:08:17.459 --> 00:08:18.292
and people are gonna say,

00:08:18.292 --> 00:08:20.607
"Well, gee, Yale, I see
Yale out there a lot.

00:08:20.607 --> 00:08:21.987
"Do we really wanna do something

00:08:21.987 --> 00:08:23.680
"that's gonna infringe on that?"

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:26.090
So, the licenses not only bring in royalty

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.890
to the University, but
also prevents the license

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:29.890
from being abused.

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:31.050
And, as an example of that,

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:34.180
like I say, we had 144 misuses last year.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.120
This year, we've only had 72.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.360
So, it is improving, it's
never gonna be perfect.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.370
It's almost like Whac-A-Mole
sometimes, the number

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.850
of issues we get.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.640
So, it's important that we continue

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:47.230
to market the brand,
license it appropriately,

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.610
and that is actually a
protection, an umbrella

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.570
for the Yale brand.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:53.383
So licensing, what exactly is licensing?

00:08:53.383 --> 00:08:56.650
There's a lot of questions
to it of how does it work,

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:59.780
what's the purpose of it,
and how is it managed?

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:04.410
Licensing at Yale is
Yale allows a company,

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:08.800
let's say Champion
Sportswear, to use its name

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.810
to market the Champion
and Yale brand together

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:14.560
and pays a royalty to the University.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.260
That royalty goes back to the University,

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.110
into the student scholarship funds.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:20.580
So, not only do we do a service

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.870
by marketing it through
a particular brand,

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.000
but we also do a service
by bringing cash back

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.470
into the University.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.800
We're actually one of the few

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.620
totally self-sufficient
departments in the entire college.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:32.940
We don't take any money from Yale.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:36.600
Everything we make, salaries,
benefits, et cetera, all come

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:37.840
from licensing revenue.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.670
We are employees of Yale, of
course, but we take our money

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:43.230
from the actual deals that we are able

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.393
to pull together within licensing.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.410
So, one of the things we do,

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:50.430
and we're actually trying to
be a little bit more aggressive

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:53.450
in that, is how do you get the
Yale name out there globally?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.330
I mean, you look out there,

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:58.412
the most popular collegiate
brand in the world is UCLA.

00:09:58.412 --> 00:10:00.361
You would not believe that, but it is.

00:10:00.361 --> 00:10:04.950
UCLA actually has 31 UCLA
stores in China itself.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.480
The issue is people, and
same thing in Europe,

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:11.450
people don't understand
that UCLA is a university.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:13.110
They just think it's a logo.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.350
So, you think about that, how
much money they're making just

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.870
because they think their brand is a logo.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.900
Couple that with the power
of our brand, the power

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:22.860
of the education behind Yale,

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.960
and it makes us a powerful entity

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.210
that we want to get out
there and tell people about.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.020
Not the way UCLA does, but to truly speak

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.300
to the essence of Yale.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:33.260
So, how do you do that?

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.250
We've done this a couple of ways.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:40.070
We now, as a university,
aggressively attend all licensing

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.600
or major licensing shows
throughout the world.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.790
We just came back from the
Las Vegas Licensing Expo,

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.390
which is the largest in the world,

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.925
over 40,000 people attended,

00:10:47.925 --> 00:10:50.530
we were the only university there.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.280
Next month, I'm gonna
be traveling to Mumbai.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.430
I'm gonna be doing the
licensing show in Mumbai.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:57.450
Our booth is gonna be
right next to Oxford's.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.220
End of next month, I'm gonna
be traveling to Shanghai

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.010
to do the Shanghai licensing show.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.090
We'll be right next to Cambridge.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.440
And, in October, we'll be
doing the Brand Licensing Expo

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:09.030
in Europe to secure
brands in that continent.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.440
So, we take a very aggressive approach

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.600
to get the Yale brand out
there internationally,

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.680
and also do protection
of it and licensing of it

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.640
from a domestic perspective.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.887
So, when we're pitching a license

00:11:18.887 --> 00:11:21.750
for a particular company,
how do you do that?

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.377
How do you say to somebody,

00:11:23.377 --> 00:11:24.530
"Hey, do you want the Yale brand?"

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.670
Or they say to you, "Can
I have the Yale brand?"

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.400
It's a very interesting dichotomy

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.940
because I would say 75% of
the time, people come to us

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:32.773
to ask for use.

00:11:32.773 --> 00:11:34.310
"Can we use the Yale brand?"

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:37.370
Well, yes you can, but there's
parameters that go around it.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.820
We have to understand
the quality of the brand.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:42.310
We have to understand what
kind of company you have.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.010
We have to understand
that a, social rights.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.030
Every licensee at Yale University has

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:50.920
to be a member of the
Fair Labor Association

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.560
to ensure that they are
protecting the workers,

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.310
no matter where they are in the world.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.480
And one thing that we're
actually very proud of,

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.510
last year, or was it, I
guess it was two years ago,

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.740
there was an issue with
one of our licensees,

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.840
and I'm proud to say it was
Yale, Cornell, Georgetown,

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.060
and the University of
Washington actually put pressure

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.080
on this very large brand
to change their ways

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.350
in Vietnam and it worked.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.030
And that brand was Nike.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:14.310
Nike does not want to hear
that Yale pulled away from them

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.620
because they're doing
something illegal overseas.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.310
So, I'm proud of the fact that Yale has

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:22.840
that, I guess, check and balance

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.790
to make sure you don't
run into those problems,

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:28.040
and if we do, we have the help
of the Fair Labor Association

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.860
to deal with that.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:31.340
So, when we're pitching to a brand,

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:34.080
or a brand's pitching to us,
I'm gonna give you an idea

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.920
of how we do that and how we speak to that

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:39.350
and how it then becomes a partnership

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.780
with us as the licensing partner.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:45.220
Revenue of the University,
marketing of the Yale brand.

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:47.090
So, the first thing you
want to do is, you want

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:48.750
to tell them about the University.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:51.150
What they love to hear
about is the history

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:53.270
and the panache of an
Ivy League institution.

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:56.713
Founded in 1701, renowned
Ivy League institution.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:12:59.350
What's the Yale mission?

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.890
And we explain the Yale mission,

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:03.330
but also how does licensing products speak

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:04.180
to that Yale mission?

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:07.750
It does because it helps to
serve and promote the brand

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.063
throughout the world.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.531
And, of course, they want
to see what Yale looks like,

00:13:12.531 --> 00:13:14.680
'cause if I'm in Mumbai or I'm in Shanghai

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.737
or Las Vegas, people
have an envision of Yale,

00:13:16.737 --> 00:13:18.290
but what is it really like?

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.320
So, being able to show potential licensees

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.260
what it looks like, you
get the wow factor and say,

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.617
"Wow, I really want to be
associated with that university.

00:13:26.617 --> 00:13:28.457
"I was right to come
to the licensing booth

00:13:28.457 --> 00:13:30.037
"and try to get that brand."

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.150
So, Yale by the numbers,

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:35.540
and the next question you
always get when you're talking

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.047
to a potential licensee
is, "Well, how big is Yale?

00:13:38.047 --> 00:13:39.247
"How many people go to Yale?

00:13:39.247 --> 00:13:41.290
"What's the alumni?"

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:43.720
So that type of
information, very important.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.610
And the thing that people always look at,

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:48.217
we have 144,000 living alumni, globally.

00:13:48.217 --> 00:13:50.560
That's very important,
especially if you're speaking

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.193
to somebody overseas.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.910
Athletics plays a huge role at Yale.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.570
If you think about all the
licenses that we have here,

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:03.480
about 144 licenses globally,
the largest ones are related

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.080
to athletics, primarily
Champion, Under Armour,

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:06.983
and so forth.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.823
We speak to the teams
that are related to that.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.180
We speak to, of course,
the Harvard-Yale game,

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:15.680
which everyone wants to be a part of,

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:18.520
because when you got 60
or 70,000 people at Yale

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.003
for a weekend, how great
is that for a brand?

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.250
And, of course, who came to Yale?

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.600
Of course, the Bushes came to Yale,

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:26.970
the Clintons came to Yale, they love

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.663
to hear stories about that.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.300
Handsome Dan.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.570
You would think that,
okay, he's a Bulldog.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.070
Well, the Bulldog's from 1889.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:38.310
It's the oldest mascot
in the United States.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.400
It was so important

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.970
that our Japanese agent
actually did a whole program

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:46.480
of Yale vintage products
based on Handsome Dan.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.507
It was very, very successful,

00:14:47.507 --> 00:14:49.600
and now we're spreading
that to other countries,

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.403
including Korea and mainland China.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:56.010
What does the Yale brand mean?

00:14:56.010 --> 00:15:00.130
What the Yale brand means
is a promise of excellence.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.660
When you think of Yale,
what do you think about?

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.440
You think about excellent education.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.590
Well, we want the product to
speak of excellence, also.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.590
Only the finest quality,
only the best factories,

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.900
only the best names, in order to make sure

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.530
that we are presenting Yale in a manner

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.080
that it should be presented in.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.980
The logos and word marks, most popular.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:23.050
On the left, the University
logo institutional mark.

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:26.330
That is reserved for what we
call some better products.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.710
It is the Yale University logo itself,

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:30.590
and you don't see that
as much as you see some

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:31.860
of the other ones.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.750
The athletic mark is actually being played

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:34.970
down a little bit recently,

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:37.063
so it's not as popular as it was.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:41.480
The most popular word
mark is the Yale block.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.520
You are going to see that, probably,

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.390
on 75% of the items that are out there

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:45.690
that are licensed by Yale.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:51.130
Other word marks, the "Y,"
Yale Bulldogs, Yale University.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:51.963
But the interesting thing is,

00:15:51.963 --> 00:15:54.580
when you think Yale University,
that would be a big play?

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.440
It really is only a big play in Asia.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:59.270
It's actually, only the
Japanese market actually uses

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.120
that for product right now,
as well as the United States.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.040
Vintage logos.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.110
This is becoming a real trend
in the market right now.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.390
You go to any college store

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.470
that carries collegiate
products right now,

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.870
that whole vintage look,
the look that went back

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:18.640
to the 50s and 60s, becoming
very important again.

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.490
So, you'll see that the leaning Bulldog,

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:23.270
the golf course logo, the
script Yale University,

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:25.650
which we just used for a
program in the United States,

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.713
and Established 1701.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.840
Now, licensing at Yale.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.590
What exactly do we offer or can we offer

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.820
to somebody who wants to
work with our institution?

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:38.203
Whoops, there we go.

00:16:39.928 --> 00:16:43.350
We want them to share a
vision of product excellence.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.200
Only the finest quality.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:46.710
We take a global approach.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:47.757
We just don't want to say,

00:16:47.757 --> 00:16:49.500
"Hey, we'll take your license,
we'll take your money."

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.060
No, that's not the way it works.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.860
The idea is that we want to work with you

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.900
to make it successful for the
licensee, make it successful

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:57.330
for the marketing of the Yale brand,

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.030
and make it successful for the revenue

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.750
that we're going to bring
into the institution.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.630
And the idea of it is we are one

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.440
of the most prestigious
universities in the world,

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:09.440
and the amount of materials,
the array of materials

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.890
that you have that you can use

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:13.170
to actually enhance the Yale brand,

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.693
as per a licensing perspective, is huge.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.920
Now, in the United States,

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.760
we have roughly 140 domestic
licensees, you see some

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.030
of the main ones there,
largest being Champion.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:27.230
Under Armor, of course,
has our sideline deal,

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.610
so you see that when you
go to football games.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:32.120
Nike used to have the sideline
deal, doesn't any longer,

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.770
but still a good, big player.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:35.560
Vineyard Vines.

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:37.940
We're the only university
in the United States

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:40.330
to have a collegiate
license with Lululemon.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.980
And also 47 Brand, who does
all, a lot of headwear,

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.363
especially for the Major League Baseball.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:47.663
Now, some of the companies

00:17:47.663 --> 00:17:50.340
that we do business with, you
think that, okay, yeah, Yale's

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.710
in the book store, Yale's
in Campus Customs, Yale's

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.810
with some other stores downtown.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:55.870
Actually, that's not the truth.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.500
Actually, Yale is all over the country

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.410
in stores that you wouldn't expect.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.280
We were in Neiman Marcus this year, we're

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.620
in PacSun right now, we were
in Barneys, every year we're

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:05.950
in Forever 21.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.030
Dick's Sporting Goods, Fanatics.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:10.370
So, it's not just downtown Broadway,

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.090
it's actually a national program
here in the United States

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:15.393
with a lot of major retailers.

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.530
Now, around the world, we also revamped

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.130
our entire licensing
program around the world

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:23.420
in order to have as a global hand

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:26.960
in all major markets, includes
the Middle East, Europe,

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:30.650
and Russia, Hong Kong, mainland China,

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:33.270
Japan, Southeast Asia, and in Canada.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.820
Actually, Canada's growing
nicely for us right now.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:38.830
Now, who do we work with around the world?

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.440
You wouldn't expect these brands
to be associated with Yale,

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:42.880
but they are.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.380
Champion Japan, we just
signed Champion Japan.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:47.455
That was a major program
based on the success

00:18:47.455 --> 00:18:50.370
of Champion United States,
and we're now working

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.050
and negotiating with Champion Taiwan.

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:56.350
Two years ago, we had a
global program with Zara.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.220
Over 2,400 stores worldwide.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.570
This year, we had a global
program with Calvin Klein.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:02.920
Now, you wouldn't think
Calvin Klein and Yale,

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:04.110
but actually, we did.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.350
Actually, we were a global
program with Calvin Klein,

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:10.300
and we actually presented at a runway

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.810
in Milan last July of Yale product,

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:15.170
along with the University of
California all pulled together,

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:16.863
which was very, very successful.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.727
Now, how do you grow that,
you have to think about it,

00:19:19.727 --> 00:19:20.847
and one of the questions you get,

00:19:20.847 --> 00:19:23.350
"Well, how do you choose which
license you want to use?"

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.250
Well, you have to take
a more global approach.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:27.750
Who's the best one you want to work with?

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.030
Okay, if you work with Calvin Klein,

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:31.570
so that creates an umbrella for the brand.

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.760
Zara, your fast fashion.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:36.050
But you also don't want
to walk away from somebody

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:39.740
who is maybe at the opening
price point, like a Primark.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.910
We do business, which is
a London-based company.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.100
We also do business
with Winners in Canada.

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:45.870
We do business with Wal-Mart.

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:47.423
The thought is here is,

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:51.700
we have t-shirts in Wal-Mart right now,

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:54.027
and you say to yourself, "Is that Yale?

00:19:54.027 --> 00:19:56.400
"Is that who Yale wants to present to?"

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:57.810
Well, actually, it is.

00:19:57.810 --> 00:19:59.480
'Cause you think about it,
there's gonna be people

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:01.910
in this world who'll never see
the Yale University campus.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.060
They'll only see it on
TV, they may never be able

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.000
to get to Yale.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.190
But, by having a t-shirt

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:07.063
at the opening price
point makes them feel like

00:20:07.063 --> 00:20:09.250
they're a part of one of
the most famous universities

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:11.910
in the world, and we're inspired by that

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:12.960
and we believe in that.

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.980
So, that's why we also
sell to your Wal-Marts

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.630
of the world, your Zaras of the world,

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.793
and we carry the brand of Calvin Klein.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:20.900
And how we break down?

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:21.900
It jumped a little bit,

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.570
but that big, blue area
is actually apparel

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.733
as the largest part, as you would imagine.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.060
And within that, again, this
slide jumped a little bit,

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.780
but men's apparel represents
about 2/3 of the apparel

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:33.613
that we do.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:35.600
And this jumped a little bit, too.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.480
In the non-apparel, the
largest area would be

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:41.450
in school products, such as
back-to-school backpacks,

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.733
paper goods, et cetera.

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:46.090
Recent licensing programs in Yale, just

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.310
to give you an idea of some of the things

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:49.840
that have happened recently
for us, to give you an idea

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:51.483
of where we're taking the brand.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.600
The Yale Co-Op Shirt.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.530
I don't know how many people
remember the old Co-Op Shirt

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:57.010
from Gant years and years ago.

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:59.110
It's been around since 1949.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.360
Gant decided they didn't want to work

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.610
with us anymore back in 2014.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.720
We've now relaunched that
through Vineyard Vines

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:05.700
and that's the ad that ran

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.453
in the alumni magazine this past month.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:12.410
Lululemon, as I mentioned,
we're the only university

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.920
in the United States to
carry the Lululemon brand,

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:15.873
and vice versa.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.640
Forever 21, we run a program every year

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:21.940
with Forever 21, extremely popular.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.840
This is the one that we ran this fall.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:26.850
And Calvin Klein.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:30.350
This product ranged anywhere
from a few dollars up

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.020
to over $2,000 for the product,

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:33.350
depending what you purchased.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.570
That cashmere, that coat
all the way on the left

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:38.400
that the young man's wearing,
that's a $25 cashmere coat.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.430
They produced only six of them worldwide

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:42.283
and sold them primarily in Europe.

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:46.010
And, of course, Zara,
this was the global brand

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:47.903
that we did with Zara two years ago.

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:51.270
And just some other examples
for you to see here.

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:52.950
These are some things that
are going on right now.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.410
You see your traditional
Yale look on the left.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:57.680
You see the leaning
Bulldog, part of PacSun,

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:00.300
and the other two, that's
actually JCPenney's website.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:01.560
We're not carrying the
store, but we're actually

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:05.330
on JCPenney's website, which
speaks very highly of us.

